    "sinoVietnameseComparison": "Because Vietnam's 2020 Enterprise Law progressively normalized digital signatures and corporate autonomy over seal design, many Vietnamese buyers become complacent when receiving PDF contracts bearing only an English signature and an oval 'English-only' stamp lacking legal validity in China. By contrast, a defensible China B2B contract requires a bilingual text designating the Chinese version as controlling for judicial accuracy (preventing technical mistranslations in PRC courts), a circular red Company Chop whose Chinese corporate name matches NECIPS 100%, and payment remitted strictly to the mainland corporate bank account—or a Hong Kong account formally authorized in writing under the parent company's Company Chop.",
