    "conclusion": "Spanning three millennia from the Book of Songs to the Four Great Classical Novels and contemporary writing, Chinese literature owes its vitality to never ossifying within a single canon, continually renewing itself through dialogue between elite scholarship and urban popular imagination. For Vietnamese scholars and students, studying Chinese literature both unlocks a vast classical archive and illuminates the creative agency with which generations of Vietnamese masters—from Nguyễn Trãi and Nguyễn Du to modern writers—appropriated and Vietnamized it.",
