    "sinoVietnameseComparison": "Hanoi's Temple of Literature–Imperial Academy (founded in 1070 under Lý Thánh Tông, with the Quốc Tử Giám established in 1076) and its 82 Doctorates' Stelae mounted on stone tortoises (inscribed into UNESCO's Memory of the World in 2011) demonstrate that Đại Việt forged public higher education and an ethos of scholarly devotion alongside China nearly a millennium ago. Notably, Vietnam's tortoise-and-crane visual symbolism carries an indigenous aesthetic signature distinct from the square-plinth tortoise stelae of Beijing's Guozijian. In 2025–2026, both nations confront strikingly parallel educational challenges: Vietnam's Grade 10 and National High School exams mirror the cram-school pressures of China's Zhongkao and Gaokao, while rising cohorts of Vietnamese students pursuing CSC, CIS, and joint tech–commerce degrees in China serve as a vital bilingual Chinese–Vietnamese–English talent bridge between the two neighboring economies.",
