    "comparativeAnalysis": "While Japanese Kimono standardized around wide o-sode/kosode sleeves cinched by a broad fixed obi sash, and Korean Hanbok fixed its silhouette on a cropped jeogori jacket over a voluminous high-waisted chima skirt, Chinese Hanfu is distinguished by dynamic shifts in silhouette and length across dynasties—moving fluidly among Ruqun, Shenyi, round-collar robes, and Mamianqun.",
