    "sinoVietnameseComparison": "Vietnam possesses centuries-old craft villages and heritage houses—such as Chu Đậu ceramics, Phú Quốc fish sauce, Vạn Phúc silk, and the traditional herbal pharmacies of Lãn Ông Street in Hanoi—yet it has not instituted a state-level accreditation regime with periodic delisting comparable to China's 'Lǎozìhào' system. China's Guócháo renaissance (and parallel Vietnamese efforts weaving Đông Sơn and Lý–Trần motifs into contemporary design) shows that artisanal goods win over younger consumers only when heritage storytelling is matched by standardized packaging and QR-verified provenance.",
