    "sinoVietnameseComparison": "Vietnam went beyond passive reception to actively localize the Stem–Branch calendar and Yijing correlative systems: most famously, the Vietnamese zodiac substitutes the Cat (Quý Mão) for the Chinese Rabbit (Mao) and embeds the Water Buffalo (Sửu) deep within wet-rice agrarian life. In traditional geomancy, Tả Ao Địa Lý (Vũ Đức Huyền, 15th–16th centuries) became an emblem of localized Vietnamese siting knowledge calibrated to the Red River Delta and Trường Sơn range rather than China's Loess Plateau. Even so, modern Vietnamese scholarship increasingly foregrounds the proverb 'Virtue prevails over destiny' (Đức năng thắng số) and empirical psychology over fatalistic superstition.",
    "examples": [
      "The Start of Spring (Lichun) boundary: in Four-Pillar Bazi, a child born before the exact solar hour of Lichun (February 4–5) retains the previous year's Stem–Branch pillar even after the first day of the Lunar New Year—proving that Ziping Bazi operates strictly on the solar terms.",
      "Cross-auditing North–South readings of a single chart: comparing Life Palace traits in Zi Wei, seasonal Five-Phase thermal balance in Bazi, and practical daylight/ventilation ergonomics in an actual workspace eliminates fear-driven, arbitrary predictions."
    ],
    "conclusion": "Honoring the historical and semiotic heritage of the Sexagenary Cycle while upholding critical scientific reasoning offers the most civilized and intellectually rigorous approach to classical shushu traditions.",
