        "heading": "1. Institutional Formality & Rank-Based Relationships in North China (Beijing, Tianjin, Hebei)",
        "body": "North China counterparties—particularly central state-owned enterprises (央企) and infrastructure conglomerates—place heavy emphasis on institutional legitimacy, rank parity (对等 Duìděng), and macro-policy alignment. Avoid aggressive price-cutting too early in initial meetings; invest instead in organizational credibility, trusted letters of introduction, and proper formal banquet protocol."
