    "theoreticalFramework": "This study combines Edward T. Hall's High-Context / Low-Context Communication framework with Regional Institutional Logics analysis. While all Chinese business regions share a Confucian substrate of 'Face' (面子 Miànzi) and relational networks (关系 Guānxì), decision weights diverge sharply between the politico-administrative axis (Beijing prioritizing formal introduction letters and rank parity at the table) and the commercial-market axis (Shanghai modeling TCO and SLAs clause by clause; Shenzhen turning around physical prototypes within 48 hours).",
