        "heading": "5. Four Policy Priorities for Hanoi, Ho Chi Minh City & Vietnam's Key Economic Regions",
        "body": "From benchmarking the five sub-regions, four highly actionable priorities emerge for Vietnam: (1) design genuine tax super-deductions for substantive R&D spending by private firms and domestic conglomerates; (2) build hard freight-rail links connecting industrial zones directly to deep-water ports (Lạch Huyện and Cái Mép–Thị Vải), mirroring the Greater Bay Area's Yantian–Shekou port network; (3) upgrade STEM education and joint university–industry laboratories in Hanoi, Đà Nẵng, and Ho Chi Minh City; and (4) shift FDI evaluation criteria from 'billions of USD in registered capital' to 'technology localization rates and binding linkages with Vietnamese domestic suppliers.'"
