        "translationEn": "The white sun sinks behind the mountain ridges; the Yellow River surges into the sea. Wishing to exhaust a thousand miles of sight, climb one story higher up the tower.",
        "source": "Wang Zhihuan (王之涣), 'Climbing Stork Tower' (《登鹳雀楼》, High Tang regulated quatrain) — Demonstrates how Sino-Vietnamese preserves the crisp entering-tone stops in bạch (白), nhật (日), nhập (入), dục (欲), and mục (目) lost in modern Mandarin."
