    "sinoVietnameseComparison": "No other Sinospheric language preserves simultaneously as rich a tonal inventory and all six Middle Chinese consonantal codas (-m, -n, -ng, -p, -t, -k) in such tight correspondence with Tang–Song Chinese as Vietnamese. Whereas Japanese On'yomi lost phonemic tones and inserted epenthetic vowels after -p/-t/-k, and Korean Hanja lost tones while shifting -t to -l, Sino-Vietnamese retains both the Yin–Yang (upper–lower register) tonal split and the stop codas -p/-t/-c. The foundational scholarship of Professors Nguyễn Tài Cẩn and Phan Ngọc remains essential reading for advanced students of classical Chinese in Vietnam.",
