    "theoreticalFramework": "Three analytical frames for reading the Hundred Schools, following Sima Tan's 'On the Essentials of the Six Schools' (Lun Liujia Yaozhi): (1) Confucianism and Mohism address communal morality and social ethics; (2) Legalism restructures power around Law (Fa), Technique (Shu), and Authority (Shi); and (3) Daoism and the Yin-Yang school synthesize the natural principle of non-coercive action (wuwei) to temper the excesses of artificial institutions.",
