    "sinoVietnameseComparison": "Owing to their vast shared Sino-Vietnamese lexical stratum, Vietnamese speakers enjoy an immediate natural advantage in reading public signage: for example, `急诊 (Jízhěn – Cấp chẩn)` corresponds to Emergency Department, `增值税发票 (Zēngzhíshuì fāpiào – Tăng trị thuế phát phiếu)` to Value-Added Tax Invoice, and `人工通道 (Réngōng tōngdào – Nhân công thông đạo)` to the manual inspection lane for foreign passport holders (as opposed to automated lanes reserved for Chinese national ID cards). Nevertheless, learners must remain alert to Sino-Vietnamese 'false friends' whose meanings diverged completely: `便宜 (piányi)` means 'inexpensive' (not 'convenient', *tiện nghi*), `手纸 (shǒuzhǐ)` means 'toilet paper' (not 'handwritten note'), and `酒店 (jiǔdiàn)` means 'hotel' (not 'wine shop' or 'liquor tavern').",
