        "body": "Understanding this shared yet divergent history explains why Vietnamese and Chinese entrepreneurs often find immediate rapport in valuing family ties, personal trustworthiness (xìn), and tea-table negotiation, while cautioning against the complacent assumption that both sides think identically. Discerning what belongs to shared East Asian heritage and what reflects distinct national culture is a core intercultural competency for International Business students."
