    "comparativeAnalysis": "Traditional Chinese architecture operates through a continuous dialogue between two value systems: (1) Confucian order in the public sphere (central-axis symmetry and status-graded proportions across the Forbidden City and Siheyuan courtyards), and (2) Daoist–Chan spontaneity in the private sphere (sinuous pathways, 'borrowed scenery' framing distant hills and pagodas, and compositions of Taihu rocks and still water in Suzhou's gardens).",
